  "model_selection_rationale": {
    "architecture": "Option A: Standardized Random Forest at Every Stage",
    "rationale": "The initial architecture selected champions strictly by Macro-F1. However, because Macro-F1 assigns equal weight to the transitional 'Enrolled' class (~18% of cohort), boosted models gained ~0.024 Macro-F1 only by predicting 'Enrolled' more aggressively, at the direct expense of dropping 4.5 to 4.8 percentage points of Dropout Recall. To align with the primary mission of early-warning dropout intervention, Option A adopts Random Forest across all three stages. Random Forest achieves the highest dropout recall and accuracy at Stages 1 and 2, matches XGBoost at Stage 3, provides direct TreeSHAP explainability, and simplifies deployment."
  }
}